From 1c30fb07b71c81b1d7dfac67bf6123bfb03e1bf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:39:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST War: SiegeArmy fix: cities build the optional
 slots of an attack it holds back

CvPlayerAI::PeekAtNextUnitToBuildForOperationSlot only served required slots,
so the optional-slot requests SiegeArmy added were dropped and no city ever
built for a waiting attack (bully pair 0714EFCB: Songhai's op 1713 waited 21
turns at 16 of 86 a turn; Economy found no 'Operation unit' entry in any
Songhai city). IsArmyTooWeakForTarget is false unless SiegeArmy is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZizcmgfGkXsgJcVcF7h
---
 CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvPlayerAI.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvPlayerAI.cpp b/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvPlayerAI.cpp
index fb434f122..c10e951dc 100644
--- a/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvPlayerAI.cpp
+++ b/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvPlayerAI.cpp
@@ -1325,7 +1325,9 @@ OperationSlot CvPlayerAI::PeekAtNextUnitToBuildForOperationSlot(CvCity* pCity, b
 			if (!pThisArmy || !pThisArmy->GetSlotStatus(thisSlot.m_iSlotID)->IsFree())
 				continue;
 
-			if (OperationalAIHelpers::IsSlotRequired(GetID(), thisSlot))
+			//AI_AB_TEST (candidate, flag SiegeArmy): an attack SiegeArmy holds back as too weak also gets its optional slots
+			//built; otherwise its requests are dropped here and the army never grows (a test game: 21 turns at 16 of 86 a turn)
+			if (OperationalAIHelpers::IsSlotRequired(GetID(), thisSlot) || pThisOperation->IsArmyTooWeakForTarget(pThisArmy))
 			{
 				bestSlot = thisSlot;
 				break;
-- 
